  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Paraguay Mother &amp; Child Basic Health Insurance</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall Project development objective is to contribute to the reduction of Paraguay&apos;s maternal and infant mortality by increasing the use of selected life-saving services included in the MCBI by women of clhid-bearing age and children under age six in Project Areas. To achieve this objective, the Project would help to; (i) create and implement the MCBI Program; (ii) improve quality and efficiency of the health service network in the Project Areas; (iii) increase the MSPBS&apos;s management capacity and transform the operational culture of the health care system to a system that rewards providers for increasing health care coverage and increasing productivity; and (iv) increase the population&apos;s participation in the social monitoring of basic and first-referral health services in the Project Areas.</narrative>
  </description>
